    "created_at": "2018-08-03T19:08:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-03T19:08:36Z",
    "body": "I have a drawing app that also allows panning and zooming.  When drawing, I want as low latency as possible, ideally by writing directly to a single-buffered hardware overlay.  When panning and zooming, I want atomic updates to prevent tearing.  Can the behavior of a canvas be changed at run-time or only when created?\r\n\r\nIf it's only possible when created, is there a way to share GL resources (VBO, FBO, etc.) across contexts to enable switching from a single-buffered canvas to a composited canvas?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
